esistant to wear and chemicals.","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04706","text":"Durable and good resistance to corrosion.","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04707","text":"It offers not only great electrical- and thermal insulation properties.","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Warping and shrinkage","items":[{"id":"Q04708","text":"Reducing shrinkage / warping","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04709","text":"Increasing dimensional stability","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04710","text":"Its low shrinkage factor and perfect layer adhesion make AthenaX GF10 a breeze to print with.","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Surface finish","items":[{"id":"Q04711","text":"Masking layer lines with a matt surface finish in 3D printed objects","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q04715","text":"PCTG is moderately hygroscopic and therefore it is recommended to pre-dry the filament at 75°C for approximately 24 hours before usage for optimal results.","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04716","text":"For optimal print results we recommend to print AthenaX GF10 filament from a drying box to avoid that the material can accumulate humidity from the environment.","source":"S-PET-TDS-AthenaX-GF10","at":"p. 2","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Nozzle wear","items"